<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnentius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">303–353</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magnentius was a Roman usurper who seized power in the West in January 350 after the murder of Emperor Constans, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. He was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> at the Battle of Mursa in 351, one of the bloodiest battles of the century, and killed himself in 353. His supporters in Britain were then harshly purged.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magnentius.jpg" alt="Magnentius" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MFA Boston · PDM-owner · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Medallion_of_Magnentius.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
